<article class="env-exercise" id="02AN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02AN">Exercise <span data-tag="02AN">111.40.8</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Show that if $R$ is a Noetherian normal domain, then $\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (R) = \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (R[t])$. [Hint: There is a map $R[t] \to R$, $t \mapsto 0$ which is a left inverse to the map $R \to R[t]$. Hence it suffices to show that any invertible $R[t]$-module $M$ such that $M/tM \cong R$ is free of rank $1$. Let $K$ be the fraction field of $R$. Pick a trivialization $K[t] \to M \otimes _{R[t]} K[t]$ which is possible by Exercise <a href="/tag/02AH" data-tag="02AH">111.40.5</a> (<a href="/tag/02AI" data-tag="02AI">1</a>). Adjust it so it agrees with the trivialization of $M/tM$ above. Show that it is in fact a trivialization of $M$ over $R[t]$ (this is where normality comes in).] 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $k$ be a field. Show that $\mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (k[x^2, x^3, t]) \not= \mathop{\mathrm{Pic}}\nolimits (k[x^2, x^3])$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>